course: dictionary
lesson: 13295
title: Grapple
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Grapple has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Read the words around it. «The two boys grappled on the wet grass, rolling over and over.» The boys are holding each other and struggling, so grapple means to fight by holding on.
explain: «Ben grappled with the long division for an hour.» Ben is not fighting anyone. Grapple with means he worked hard at a difficult problem. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "Ben worked hard at a difficult problem for an hour" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Grapple can also be a noun: «The sailor threw a grapple over the side to hold the boat.» Look for a or the in front of it. A grapple is a thing, a hook that grabs or holds something, not an action.
fact: Grapple has three meanings: to fight by holding someone, to work hard at a difficult problem, and a hook.
fact: «Grapple with» means to work hard to understand or deal with something difficult.
fact: A grapple, also called a grappling hook, is a hook used to grab or hold something.
fact: Grapples, grappled and grappling are the verb forms; «grappled» tells you it happened in the past.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The two boys grappled on the wet grass.» What does grappled mean here? | To run a race across the field | *To fight by holding and struggling with each other | To sleep on the grass
exercise: «Mia grappled with her spelling homework all evening.» What does grappled with mean? | *Worked hard to deal with something difficult | Played a game with | Ate her dinner quickly
exercise: Nadia says a grapple is a kind of bird. What is a grapple really? | A soft blanket | A small bird that sings | A type of wooden boat | *A hook used to grab or hold something
test: «The firefighters grappled with the flames until the sun came up.» What does grappled with mean? | Sang loudly to | Cooked dinner for | Ran away from | *Worked hard to deal with something difficult
test: «The pirate threw his grapple onto the ship's rail and climbed up.» What is a grapple in this sentence? | A sail | A sword | *A hook used to grab and hold | A flag
exam: «The wrestlers grappled in the ring, each trying to pin the other down.» What does grappled mean here? | Sat quietly | Waved to the crowd | Ran around the ring | *Fought by holding and struggling with each other
